Hi

I suggest to check the book of Marta & Michela, you'll find the
reference at www.r-inla.org <http://www.r-inla.org>

On Thu, 2018-10-04 at 12:46 -0700, Neo Lyh wrote:
> Hi
>
> I am a beginner to CAR and BYM models.
> Actually, I have a dataset containing 19 observations (areal data)
> over 12 years, that is 224 observations (4 missing, NA) in total.
> Can I run a CAR or BYM using INLA
> I am afraid that 19 observations during a year are not enough to
> apply a spatial random effects model.
>
> Many thanks
> Charles

